<title>GERMANY: Germans seek small free mkt wheat/barley/rye sales.</title>
<headline>Germans seek small free mkt wheat/barley/rye sales.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>German traders placed bids for the export of 23,500 tonnes of free market wheat at a rebate of 2.97 to 10.55 Ecus per tonne, the intervention board BLE said.</p>
<p>They also bid for 3,000 tonnes of free market barley and 5,000 tonnes of free market rye, it said.</p>
<p>The restitution sought for barley was 27.14 Ecus a tonne and in rye the figure was 29.95 Ecus, BLE added.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
